# Frontend Engineering Rules

## Role

Senior Next.js Frontend Engineer / UX Architect for a multi-tenant SaaS LMS.

Prioritize: clean architecture, type safety, accessibility, performance, reusability.

**Schema:** `.cursor/docs/architecture/frontend-schema.md`  
**Prompt:** `.cursor/prompts/frontend.md`

---

## Tech Stack

- Next.js App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- HeroUI v3.2.2, Tailwind CSS v4
- Better Auth + Rails JWT (`lib/auth/`)
- Wretch (`lib/api/`)
- TanStack React Query (server state)
- TanStack React Table (data grids)
- React Hook Form + Zod
- next-intl, next-themes, Sonner, Recharts
- clsx, class-variance-authority, date-fns

---

## Architecture

- Feature-based: `features/<name>/` with components, hooks, schemas, services, types
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when required
- Compose in `page.tsx` — no `<Feature>Page` wrappers
- No `AppShell`, `AuthLayout`, `DashboardLayout` wrapper components
- `components/<domain>/` for shared composites reused 3+ features
- `layout/sidebar/`, `layout/top-bar/` for dashboard chrome
- `proxy.ts` for auth/role guards; no `app/page.tsx`

---

## Data Fetching

- Use React Query hooks — not raw `useEffect` + `fetch` in components
- Feature services call `lib/api/client.ts`
- Mutations: invalidate queries + Sonner toast
- Tenant from session only — never URL `school_id`

---

## HeroUI v3

Only UI library. Use primitives directly. Forbidden: custom Button, Input, Modal, Table replacements.

---

## TypeScript

Strict mode. No `any`. Typed props, API responses, hooks.

---

## Formatting

4 spaces. Prettier. Functional components only.
